# XCU tsort
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All tests run in the POSIX locale. Output order is checked against the
# input pairs, since many orders can be valid; only chains with one valid order
# are compared exactly.

assertion  XCU.tsort.001
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       tsort writes every item once, one per line, so that the first item of each pair of different items comes before the second.
test       t/001-ordering.sh

assertion  XCU.tsort.002
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#INPUT FILES
class      required
since      1992
says       A pair of identical items only records the item; blanks and newlines in any number separate items.
test       t/002-identical-and-separators.sh

assertion  XCU.tsort.003
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#STDERR
class      required
since      2024
says       A cycle in the input is reported on standard error, and input without a cycle gives no diagnostic.
test       t/003-cycle-message.sh

assertion  XCU.tsort.004
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#OPTIONS/-w
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      2024
says       With -w the exit status is the number of cycles found, and the message is a diagnostic; with no cycle the status is 0.
test       t/004-w-option.sh

assertion  XCU.tsort.005
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#OPERANDS/file
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/tsort.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       tsort reads the file operand, else standard input; empty input gives no output and status 0; a missing file gives a nonzero status.
test       t/005-operands.sh
